jobs.description:
Job Vacancy: Office Cleaner – Arkel

Are you looking for a fun part-time job with fixed daytime hours? We are looking for an enthusiastic Cleaner for a location in Arkel. You will earn €15.52 gross per hour and have the flexibility to choose your working hours within the agreed schedule.

Working hours

- Monday, Thursday, and Friday;
- Working hours to be agreed between 7:00 AM and 1:30 PM;
- 2.5 hours per day;
- Long-term position.

No experience? No problem! You will receive thorough training from your colleagues.

Are you someone who:

- Speaks a reasonable level of Dutch or English;
- Is available for approximately 8 hours per week;
- Lives in the Gorinchem or Noordeloos area;
- Can start at short notice.

As a Logistics Employee, you will begin your journey in the Value Added Services (VAS) department. Together with your team, you ensure that products are processed accurately and prepared for shipment to customers around the world.

Your daily tasks include:

- Inspecting incoming goods;
- Loading and unloading containers;
- Labelling and repacking products where required;
- Picking, checking and preparing customer orders for shipment;

You will start in a day shift:

- Monday to Friday from 07:00 AM to 04:00 PM;
- On your first working day, you will work from 08:00 AM to 05:00 PM. You will be paired with a buddy who will guide you through the tasks and explain everything step by step.
Starting from the 2nd day you will start at 07.00 o clock in the morning.

During busy periods, you will work in a two-shift schedule:

- 06:00 AM to 03:00 PM;
- 03:00 PM to 12:00 AM.

After approximately two months, you will move to another logistics department. Here, you will learn new tasks and gain even more variety in your work. This gives you the opportunity to develop yourself into an all-round logistics employeeDo you see yourself working in a dynamic logistics environment where you can develop your skills and grow within the company? Don’t wait any longer and apply today! We will contact you as soon as possible to discuss the opportunities.

- You speak and understand English well;
- You are available to work full-time;
- You are willing to work in a two-shift schedule after your training period;
- You have experience working in logistics or production;
- You are motivated and enjoy working hands-on.
